WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Imagine a device built for PRP.

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.260
No SIM card.

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:06.660
No phone number.

4
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.700
You connect through identities and
relationships.

5
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.060
Personal life. Work.

6
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.520
Different contexts, different identities.

7
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.270
You choose who you communicate with,

8
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.380
not a number assigned by an operator.

9
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.590
A home device can arrive with its own identity,

10
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.370
created at the factory

11
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.970
without consulting an authority

12
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.860
or receiving a delegation.

13
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.740
Take it out of the box.

14
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.700
It needs no manual internet setup,

15
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.520
SIM, or manufacturer's controller.

16
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.690
Scan its printed QR code

17
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.230
to establish your relationship—

18
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:43.020
not to activate its connection.

19
00:00:44.892 --> 00:00:47.302
The same connectivity provider can serve you

20
00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:49.042
on behalf of several operators,

21
00:00:49.072 --> 00:00:51.972
across different connection technologies.

22
00:00:52.632 --> 00:00:55.692
An operator becomes one option among others,

23
00:00:56.072 --> 00:00:58.452
not the exclusive owner of your access.

24
00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.902
Your relationships are not tied

25
00:01:00.932 --> 00:01:02.312
to a single subscription.

26
00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:05.668
At home, Wi-Fi connects

27
00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.438
through your local equipment.

28
00:01:08.018 --> 00:01:09.888
Across the city, antennas provide

29
00:01:09.918 --> 00:01:11.538
metropolitan coverage.

30
00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.008
Satellite links offer another way

31
00:01:14.038 --> 00:01:15.638
to reach wider networks.

32
00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:17.998
Different equipment, different reach.

33
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:19.808
More than one way to carry

34
00:01:19.838 --> 00:01:21.118
the same relationships.

35
00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:25.168
Devices can also connect directly

36
00:01:25.198 --> 00:01:26.458
through Wi-Fi Direct.

37
00:01:27.118 --> 00:01:29.068
Subscribers can form mesh networks,

38
00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:30.468
carrying communication

39
00:01:30.498 --> 00:01:32.938
through participating neighbors.

40
00:01:33.398 --> 00:01:35.108
Each chooses whether to contribute

41
00:01:35.138 --> 00:01:36.638
and on what terms.

42
00:01:37.198 --> 00:01:39.008
The network grows through participation,

43
00:01:39.038 --> 00:01:42.018
not through a mandatory central operator.

44
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:44.580
As you move,

45
00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.090
connections and providers can change.

46
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.400
PRP separates the relationship

47
00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:51.430
from the path carrying it.

48
00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.680
Where another authorized path is available,

49
00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.230
communication can continue that way.

50
00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.480
You do not need a new phone number,

51
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.650
or to rebuild your relationships.

52
00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:05.230
The same autonomy extends to smart cities,

53
00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.020
from street equipment to flood sensors.

54
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:10.950
Across a city,

55
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.060
civil defense can reach thousands

56
00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.990
through an authorized group.

57
00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.240
PRP groupcast provides native multicast

58
00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.610
across operators:

59
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.710
the message branches through the network,

60
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.260
rather than requiring a separate send

61
00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:26.770
to every recipient.

62
00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:28.710
For field teams,

63
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.830
push-to-talk carries a speaker's voice to the
group,

64
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.970
even across different operators.

65
00:02:35.892 --> 00:02:36.432
You arrive.

66
00:02:36.952 --> 00:02:38.612
The conversation continues.

67
00:02:39.072 --> 00:02:40.332
No SIM card.

68
00:02:40.812 --> 00:02:42.202
No telephone numbering plan

69
00:02:42.232 --> 00:02:44.472
defining how people reach you.

70
00:02:44.792 --> 00:02:46.572
Identities and relationships,

71
00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.142
carried by networks you can choose

72
00:02:49.172 --> 00:02:50.382
and help build.

73
00:02:50.412 --> 00:02:54.052
Mobile, without a mandatory central operator.

74
00:02:54.532 --> 00:02:55.972
Connected, on your terms.

75
00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.122
PRP.

